Wings patch 0010: move files between the browser and the workspace

OpenManus's sandbox shares files between its browser, shell and code. Wings
now does the same, safely:

  * Downloads: the browser's downloads volume is mounted read-only inside
    the default workspace (/workspaces/default/downloads, compose), so
    read_file, python and the Workspace files page see what the browser
    downloaded.
  * Uploads: private_browser fill on a file field with path= attaches a
    workspace file (wings/browser.py; no symlinks, at most 50 MB, nothing
    outside /workspaces). src/tool_capabilities.py classifies a browser
    action carrying a path as an external side effect, so upstream's
    approval gate shows the person the exact upload before it happens.
  * src/tool_schemas.py: documents both.

Applies to: odysseus-dev/odysseus@9d0d3720f4ca181d87bef94da826d730acc6d483
